        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0000023</IRI>
        <Literal>Enoxacin belongs to a group called fluoroquinolones. Its mode of action depends upon blocking bacterial DNA replication by binding itself to DNA gyrase and causing double-stranded breaks in the bacterial chromosome.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
