        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0000079</IRI>
        <Literal>Clavulanic acid is a beta-lactamase inhibitor (marketed by GlaxoSmithKline, formerly Beecham) combined with penicillin group antibiotics to overcome certain types of antibiotic resistance. It is used to overcome resistance in bacteria that secrete beta-lactamase, which otherwise inactivates most penicillins.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
