        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000004</IRI>
        <Literal>Ambler Class B beta-lactamases are the metallo-beta-lactamases.  These enzymes possess one or two zinc ions in the active site, which are used to orient a hydroxide nucleophile to attack the carbonyl on a beta-lactam ring.  There are currently no inhibitors in late-stage development for these relatively new beta-lactamases.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
