            <Literal>PMID:18757750</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000079</IRI>
        <Literal>Oxazolidinones are a class of synthetic antibiotics discovered the the 1980&apos;s.  They inhibit protein synthesis by binding to domain V of the 23S rRNA of the 50S subunit of bacterial ribosomes.  Linezolid is the only member of this class currently in clinical use.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
