        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000123</IRI>
        <Literal>Gramicidins are a family of antibiotics synthesized by Bacillus brevis. It includes the linear pentadecapeptides gramicidin A, B and C that make up the mixture gramicidin D. Gramicidin S is a cyclic peptide chain. Gramicidins are also components of tyrothricins, another mixture of antibiotics produced by Bacillus brevis.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
