        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000128</IRI>
        <Literal>A category of aminoglycoside O-phosphotransferase enzymes with modification regiospecificity based at the 2&apos;&apos;-hydroxyl group of the respective antibiotic. These enzymes inactivate aminoglycoside antibiotics, specifically kanamycin, tobramycin and amikacin, by the ATP-dependent phosphorylation of the 3&apos;-hydroxyl group of the compound.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
