        <Literal>A thiol transferase that leads to the resistance of fosfomycin. Contrasting FosA, FosB is dependent on the cofactor Magnesium (II) and uses either bacillithiol or  L-cysteine to open up the epoxide ring of fosfomycin.</Literal>
