        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000187</IRI>
        <Literal>Mechanism of enzymatic degradation common to Ambler Class A, C and D beta-lactamases.  A serine residue located in the active site is used to form an acyl-enzyme intermediate and subsequent hydrolysis renders the beta-lactam inactive.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
