        <Literal>Macrolide phosphotransferases (MPH) are enzymes encoded by macrolide phosphotransferase genes (mph genes). These enzymes phosphorylate macrolides in GTP dependent manner at 2&apos;-OH of desosamine sugar thereby inactivating them. Characterized MPH&apos;s are differentiated based on their substrate specificity.</Literal>
