        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000384</IRI>
        <Literal>AcrAB-TolC is a tripartite RND efflux system that confers resistance to tetracycline, chloramphenicol, ampicillin, nalidixic acid, and rifampin  in Gram-negative bacteria. The system spans the cell membrane (AcrB) and the outer-membrane (TolC), and is linked together in the periplasm by AcrA.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
