        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000452</IRI>
        <Literal>Fluoroquinolones inhibit type II and type IV topoisomerases (2 strand breaking enzymes) such as GyrA/GyrB and ParC/ParE. Point mutations in the associated gyrA and parC genes, in particular in the &apos;quinolone resistance determining region&apos; (QRDR), give rise to resistance to the class.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
