        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000457</IRI>
        <Literal>ParE is a subunit of topoisomerase IV, which decatenates and relaxes DNA to allow access to genes for transcription or translation. Point mutations in ParE prevent anticoumarin antibiotics from inhibiting DNA synthesis, thus conferring resistance.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
