        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000461</IRI>
        <Literal>Florfenicol is a fluorine derivative of chloramphenicol, where the nitro group (-NO2) is substituted by a sulfomethyl group (-SO2CH3) and the hydroxyl group (-OH), by a fluorine group (-F). The action mechanism is the same as chloramphenicol&apos;s, where the antibiotic binds to the 23S RNA of the 50S subunit of bacterial ribosomes to inhibit protein synthesis.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
