        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000723</IRI>
        <Literal>D-Alanine synthetase (or ligase), also known as ddla, joins two D-alanines before their addition to the pentapeptide chains of peptidoglycan. It is found in both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
