        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000872</IRI>
        <Literal>Enoyl-acyl carrier reductases catalyze the final enoyl reduction step in bacterial type II fatty acid elongation. Triclosan antibiotics block enoyl reduction and therefore fatty acid synthesis, functioning as a broad spectrum biocide and antibiotic.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
