        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3001796</IRI>
        <Literal>OXA-50 is a beta-lactamase found in Pseudomonas aeruginosa. It confers decreased susceptibility to ampicillin and ticarcillin and, interestingly, to moxalactam and meropenem in P. aeruginosa but not in E. coli. Also confers resistance to piperacillin-tazobactam and cephalotin.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
