        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3002569</IRI>
        <Literal>AAC(6&apos;)-Iy is a chromosomal-encoded aminoglycoside acetyltransferase in S. enteritidis and S. enterica. Regulatory mutation required to increase expression of this chromosomally-encoded gene for resistance. In the specific system, aminoglycoside resistance was due to a transcriptional fusion secondary to a chromosomal deletion in which the downstream aac(6&apos;)-Iy gene was placed under the control of the upstream nmpC promoter.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
