        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3003421</IRI>
        <Literal>Catalyzes the transfer of a lysyl group from L-lysyl-tRNA(Lys) to membrane-bound phosphatidylglycerol (PG), which produces lysylphosphatidylglycerol (LPG), a major component of the bacterial membrane with a positive net charge. LPG synthesis contributes to bacterial virulence as it is involved in the resistance mechanism against cationic antimicrobial peptides (CAMP) produces by the host&apos;s immune system (defensins, cathelicidins) and by the competing microorganisms (bacteriocins).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
