        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3003733</IRI>
        <Literal>FusC is a fusidic acid resistance gene enabling ribosomal translocase EF-G dissociation from the ribosome that has been detected in Staphylococcus aureus and Staphylococcus intermedius. Its mechanism is believed to be similar to fusB due to its high level of sequence homology. It is considered a FusB-type protein.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
