        <Literal>Bulgecin A is a lytic transglycosylase inhibitor and antibiotic potentiator produced from Pseudomonas mesoacidophila. In the presence of some beta-lactam antibiotics, including ampicillin and meropenem, bulgecin A has been shown to restore susceptibility to carbapenems in carbapenem-resistant pathogens.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
