        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3004300</IRI>
        <Literal>Intermediate sensitivity of a bacterial strain to a given antibiotic occurs when it is inhibited by a concentration of the drug that is associated with uncertain therapeutic effect. The elimination of intermediate phenotype bacteria may depend on the site of infection and/or the concentration of the administered drug. Definition from https://clsi.org.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
