        <Literal>Microbes exposed to antimicrobial agents are then stained with the intercalating agent propidium iodide. Damaged cells emit a positive signal that is detected by flow cytometry analysis. Flow cytometry can also be used to discriminate between dead, damaged and live cells.</Literal>
