        <Literal>PNGM is a family of metallo-beta-lactamases first identified from a deep-sea sediment metagenome and shown to reduce antibiotic susceptibility by hydrolysis of penicillins, carbapenems and extended- and broad-spectrum cephalosporins.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
