        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3004577</IRI>
        <Literal>AmvA has 14 alpha-helical transmembrane segments, qualifying it as a member of the DHA2 transporter family of the major facilitator superfamily (MFS). When AmvA was expressed in E. coli,  the cells had at least four-fold decreased susceptibility to erythromycin, acridine orange, acriflavine, deoxycholate and methyl viologen. AmvA from the AC0037 strain of A. baumannii was tested.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
