        <Literal>The 30S ribosomal protein S1 of Mycobacterium tuberculosis is required for mRNA translation initiation, playing a particular role in trans-translation. Mutations to rpsA prevent pyrazinoic acid, the active form of pyrazinamide catalyzed by pncA, from targeting RpsA to inhibit translation.</Literal>
