        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007093</IRI>
        <Literal>Klebsidin is a peptide antibiotic derived from Klebsiella pneumoniae that exhibits activity against members of the Enterobacteriaceae family of Gram-negative bacteria, including Escherichia and Salmonella species. Klebsidin acts by accumulating in the target cell and inhibiting RNA polymerase.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
