        <Literal>Fisetin is a flavonoid produced mainly by plants in the Eudicotidae clade. It exhibits a range of biological activities such as anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties, and fisetin has been shown to inhibit the action of metallo-beta-lactamases.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
