        <Literal>Phenylalanine-arginine beta-naphthylamide is a widely-used experimental efflux pump inhibitor. It has also been shown to increase Gram-negative membrane permeability and enhance the entry of antibiotics, even in efflux pump deficient strains. It is also able to inhibit the formation of bacterial biofilms and disrupt quorum sensing.</Literal>
