        <Literal>ampR is a regulatory gene that plays an essential role in regulating antibiotic resistance in P. aeruginosa. Mutation in ampR leads to its loss of control over blaPDC-16, allowing overexpression of blaPDC-16 and further resistance to aztreonam.</Literal>
