        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007540</IRI>
        <Literal>Cyclomarins are cyclic heptapeptides containing four unusual amino acids. Cyclomarins target two different targets: Clp C1, a subunit of the caseinolytic protease of Mycobacterium tuberculosis (MTB), and PfAp3Ase of Plasmodium falciparum. Therefore, cyclomarins are interesting lead structures for the development of drugs against tuberculosis and malaria.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
