        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007541</IRI>
        <Literal>Cyclomarin A was found to be bacteriocidal against bacteria replicating in culture broth and in human-derived macrophages and a series of multidrug resistant clinical isolates. It was identified as a potent antitubercular compound in a natural product whole cell screen. Importantly it kills both growing and dormant, non-replicating mycobacteria.</Literal>
