        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007679</IRI>
        <Literal>Chrysomycin A (ChryA) is a benzonaphthopyranone glycoside with rapid bactericidal activity that is highly active against S. aureus persisters, robustly eradicates biofilms in vitro, and shows a sustainable killing efficacy in vivo. Chrysomycin A belongs to the coumarin class of antibiotics which are known to bind gyrase subunit B and inhibit the enzyme function.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
